# PHASE 11 — ARCHITECTURE, RELIABILITY AND SECURITY

Implement the following where appropriate to the existing architecture:

- Idempotent ingestion and event-level deduplication.
- Retry handling and rate-limit-aware RPC access.
- WebSocket reconnect and backfill mechanisms.
- Cursor/checkpoint-based ingestion recovery.
- Transaction and block ordering appropriate to each chain.
- Explicit finality and data-completeness states.
- Versioned normalized event schemas.
- Indexed persistence for signatures, addresses, mints, authorities and timestamps.
- Separation of ingestion, decoding, enrichment, detection and presentation.
- Structured logging, health metrics and error reporting.
- Secure secret management and server-side API keys.
- Input validation and safe rendering of untrusted blockchain data.
- Role-based access and auditable analyst actions where supported.
- Backward-compatible migrations and configuration defaults.

Do not store secrets in frontend code or commit API keys.

Do not silently discard unsupported instructions or failed transactions.

Do not mark incomplete investigations as complete.

Do not allow an AI explanation or an inferred risk score to alter authoritative on-chain evidence.

Any automated remediation, transaction submission, account freezing or external response action must be separately authorised, policy-controlled and auditable. Default to read-only analysis.

